Rampart, whose own name was Viktor Kozlovsky, was an orc man of [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/index|Oresk]] and an officer of [[Org/Althane/The First House|the First House]] at its ultra-violet rank, serving in its regalia. He was a heavy, deliberate man, and magic did not touch him. His bones had been replaced with rods of adamantine shaped like them, so that his skeleton was wholly that metal, and where his heart belonged sat an engine of divine make like the ones [[Org/Althane/The Weft|the Weft]] carry, a flame hot enough to melt whatever held it. [[People/Althane/The Slipseer|The Slipseer]] is his sister.

He was seen in a room of white walls and steel floor, watching a glass tube: inside it a faint blue glow hung motionless while a reddish glow threw itself against the glass. He kept the Kaathe [[People/Althane/Halidex Op-B|Hali]] and [[People/Althane/Tennobrin Er-K|Tenno]] in the vats of [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/RC3|RC3]], and [[People/Althane/Lev|Lev]] counted him a particular enemy.

Lev killed him at RC3 and promised to send him personally to [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/Nox|Nox]]. His corpse stayed hot long after he died.
